Adverse Events (TEAEs)\",\"description\":\"TEAEs are defined as any adverse event (AE) that began or increased in severity or frequency at or after the time of first treatment up to end of study (up to Week 79). A treatment-emergent serious adverse event (SAE) was a TEAE that met at least 1 of the following criteria: was fatal, life-threatening, required or prolonged inpatient hospitalization, resulted in persistent or significant disability/incapacity, was a congenital anomaly/birth defect, or was another medically important serious event.\\n\\nThe treatment-emergent events of interest (EOI) prespecified for this study included serious infections (meningococcus aspergillus, and other serious infections/sepsis), and infusion reactions.\",\"populationDescription\":\"The safety analysis set included all treated participants, with treatment assigned based on actual treatment received.\",\"reportingStatus\":\"POSTED\",\"paramType\":\"COUNT_OF_PARTICIPANTS\",\"unitOfMeasure\":\"Participants\",\"timeFrame\":\"Day 1 to End of Study (up to Week 79)\",\"groups\":[{\"id\":\"OG000\",\"title\":\"ABP 959\",\"description\":\"Participants who received ABP 959 900 mg in Period 1 (administered IV every 14 ± 2 days for 52 weeks) or ABP 959 900 mg in Period 2 (administered IV every 14 ± 2 days for 26 weeks).\"},{\"id\":\"OG001\",\"title\":\"Eculizumab\",\"description\":\"Participants who received eculizumab 900 mg in Period 1 (administered IV every 14 ± 2 days for 52 weeks) or eculizumab 900 mg in Period 2 (administered IV every 14 ± 2 days for 26 weeks).\"}],\"denoms\":[{\"units\":\"Participants\",\"counts\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"41\"},{\"groupId\":\"OG001\",\"value\":\"42\"}]}],\"classes\":[{\"title\":\"All TEAEs\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"33\"},{\"groupId\":\"OG001\",\"value\":\"39\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Any Treatment-emergent SAE\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"7\"},{\"groupId\":\"OG001\",\"value\":\"2\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Any Treatment-emergent EOI: Infusion reaction\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"15\"},{\"groupId\":\"OG001\",\"value\":\"15\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Any Treatment-emergent EOI: Serious infection\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"3\"},{\"groupId\":\"OG001\",\"value\":\"0\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"SECONDARY\",\"title\":\"Number of Participants With Antidrug Antibodies (ADAs)\",\"description\":\"Any samples that tested positive for binding antibodies were also tested for neutralizing antibodies. Treatment boosted ADAs were defined as a positive immunoassay result at baseline and at least 1 postbaseline immunoassay result that was ≥ 4 times the magnitude of the baseline result. Baseline was defined as the last non-missing assessment taken prior to the first dose of IP.\",\"populationDescription\":\"The safety analysis set included all treated participants, with treatment assigned based on actual treatment received.\",\"reportingStatus\":\"POSTED\",\"paramType\":\"COUNT_OF_PARTICIPANTS\",\"unitOfMeasure\":\"Participants\",\"timeFrame\":\"Blood samples for ADA assessments were taken predose at baseline, Week 3, Week 7, Week 13, Week 19, Week 25, Week 27, Week 33, Week 39, Week 45, Week 51, Week 53, Week 55, Week 59, Week 65, Week 71, Week 77 and Week 79.\",\"groups\":[{\"id\":\"OG000\",\"title\":\"ABP 959/Eculizumab\",\"description\":\"Participants received ABP 959 900 mg administered IV every 14 ± 2 days for 52 weeks in Period 1 followed by eculizumab 900 mg administered IV every 14 ± 2 days for 26 weeks in Period 2.\"},{\"id\":\"OG001\",\"title\":\"Eculizumab/ABP 959\",\"description\":\"Participants received eculizumab 900 mg administered IV every 14 ± 2 days for 52 weeks in Period 1 followed by ABP 959 900 mg administered IV every 14 ± 2 days for 26 weeks in Period 2.\"}],\"denoms\":[{\"units\":\"Participants\",\"counts\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"20\"},{\"groupId\":\"OG001\",\"value\":\"22\"}]}],\"classes\":[{\"title\":\"Binding antibody positive anytime\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"0\"},{\"groupId\":\"OG001\",\"value\":\"2\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Neutralizing antibody positive anytime\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"0\"},{\"groupId\":\"OG001\",\"value\":\"0\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Binding antibody positive at/before baseline\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"0\"},{\"groupId\":\"OG001\",\"value\":\"0\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Neutralizing antibody positive at/before baseline\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"0\"},{\"groupId\":\"OG001\",\"value\":\"0\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Treatment boosted antibody positive\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"0\"},{\"groupId\":\"OG001\",\"value\":\"0\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Binding antibody positive postbaseline with negative/no result at baseline\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"0\"},{\"groupId\":\"OG001\",\"value\":\"2\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Overall: Neutralizing antibody positive postbaseline with negative/no result at baseline\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"0\"},{\"groupId\":\"OG001\",\"value\":\"0\"}]}]}]}]},\"adverseEventsModule\":{\"frequencyThreshold\":\"5\",\"timeFrame\":\"Day 1 to End of Study (up to Week 79)\",\"description\":\"All-cause mortality is reported for all participants enrolled/randomized in the study. Serious adverse events and other adverse events are reported for all participants who received at least one dose of study drug.\",\"eventGroups\":[{\"id\":\"EG000\",\"title\":\"Period 1: ABP 959\",\"description\":\"Participants received ABP 959 900 mg administered IV every 14 ± 2 days for 52 weeks in Period 1.\",\"deathsNumAffected\":0,\"deathsNumAtRisk\":20,\"seriousNumAffected\":3,\"seriousNumAtRisk\":20,\"otherNumAf